          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="40" edge="1" parent="1" source="24" style="html=1;rounded=0;edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;endFill=1;strokeColor=#3f3f52;strokeWidth=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#1c1c1c;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;endArrow=classic;exitX=1.000;exitY=0.727;exitPerimeter=0;entryX=0.000;entryY=0.444;entryPerimeter=0;endSize=6;jettySize=auto;" target="19" value="Opens with Reader roles">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="-0.5" y="-14.5" as="offset" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="100" parent="1" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f7f7ff;strokeColor=#b9b9e6;dashed=1;dashPattern=4 4;fontColor=#1c1c1c;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;Availability tests: What they Probe and Why&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Probes:&lt;/b&gt; https://&amp;lt;public host&amp;gt;/healthz.html. The public host is the Front Door endpoint, or the Static Web App default host in dev (no Front Door). Each custom domain with monitor = true gets its own test.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why /healthz.html:&lt;/b&gt; it is the only page without sign-in. Every other page redirects to the Entra login, so a test on / would only prove the redirect works.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;How:&lt;/b&gt; Application Insights Standard web tests from 5 Azure locations (Amsterdam, Dublin, Moscow, Virginia, Singapore), every 5 minutes, 30 s timeout, one retry, GET following redirects.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Passes when:&lt;/b&gt; HTTP 200, and a valid TLS certificate with more than 14 days left.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Path tested:&lt;/b&gt; DNS → WAF → Front Door → Static Web App, the same path guests take.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Alert:&lt;/b&gt; severity 1 when availability across the locations drops below 90% over 5 minutes. Results also feed the workbook dashboard.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Does not prove:&lt;/b&gt; that sign-in works (Entra ID, app registration, client secret and guest access are not exercised; an expired secret breaks sign-in while the tests stay green), or that protected pages are served." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="270" width="700" x="20" y="945.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="101" edge="1" parent="1" source="100" style="html=1;edgeStyle=none;endArrow=none;dashed=1;dashPattern=4 4;strokeColor=#8a8781;strokeWidth=1.2;exitX=0.464;exitY=0;exitPerimeter=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=1;entryPerimeter=0;" target="13" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-2" parent="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;How guests get in, and how we know the site is up&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;What happens&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• An approved guest opens the site from anywhere; Front Door and its firewall receive the request&lt;br&gt;• Before any page is shown, the site sends them to Microsoft Entra ID to sign in with their own work or Microsoft account&lt;br&gt;• Entra lets in only members of the site&amp;#x27;s users group or another approved group&lt;br&gt;• Every 5 minutes, tests in 5 regions open the health page, the only page that needs no sign-in&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why we do it this way&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• The people are outside the company, so the site must be on the internet, but its content is not public&lt;br&gt;• Guests keep their own accounts, so there are no passwords for us to manage&lt;br&gt;• Removing someone from the group removes their access" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12;html=1;fillColor=#f7f7ff;strokeColor=#b9b9e6;dashed=1;dashPattern=4 4;fontColor=#1c1c1c;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="20.0" y="1235.0" width="700.0" height="230" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-3" parent="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;What to keep in mind&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Tests do not cover sign-in:&lt;/b&gt; an expired client secret or a broken app registration stops every guest while the availability tests stay green. The secret rotates every 180 days, but only on the next apply; an environment left unapplied for about 210 days stops signing guests in.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Hosts must match:&lt;/b&gt; the redirect URIs and allowedForwardedHosts must list every host guests see (Front Door endpoint and custom domains). Add a domain and apply before announcing it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Guest lifecycle:&lt;/b&gt; for more than a few people, the identity team invites guests and manages the group. Review the group regularly so stale guests lose access.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Outside Terraform:&lt;/b&gt; Conditional Access (MFA for guests) and cross-tenant access settings are recommended but not created here.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Standard everywhere:&lt;/b&gt; custom Entra sign-in needs the Standard Static Web App, so even dev cannot use the Free tier.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Region and zones:&lt;/b&gt; the region is the location setting, one of the 5 Static Web Apps regions. Nothing here is zonal: Front Door and the site content are global, and the Terraform state storage is zone- and geo-redundant (GZRS).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Cost:&lt;/b&gt; about $38 (dev), $73 (qa) and $368 (uat, prod) a month before traffic, at West Europe list prices. Front Door Premium ($330) is 90 % of it; guests are free up to 50,000 active users a month. The uat budget (400) is tight." style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12;html=1;fillColor=#f7f7ff;strokeColor=#b9b9e6;dashed=1;dashPattern=4 4;fontColor=#1c1c1c;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="20.0" y="1485.0" width="700.0" height="300" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-4" parent="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;Why pick this design, and its trade-offs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Entra B2B guests, not a separate identity store:&lt;/b&gt; guests use their own accounts, and access is a group membership in the tenant we already run. Trade-off: someone must invite, review and remove guests.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Assignment required, not any account:&lt;/b&gt; Entra itself refuses anyone outside an approved group, before the site sees them. Trade-off: every new person needs an invitation and a group change; no self sign-up.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Built-in sign-in, not code in the site:&lt;/b&gt; the site stays build-free HTML, CSS and JavaScript, and one config file protects every route. Trade-off: a client secret that expires if the environment is not re-applied within about 210 days.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Front Door and WAF kept:&lt;/b&gt; the site is still on the internet, so it keeps rate limiting, geo blocking and managed rules. Trade-off: same cost as the public design.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;An anonymous /healthz.html, not a test account:&lt;/b&gt; the availability tests need no credentials, which would otherwise have to be stored and rotated. Trade-off: the tests stay green while sign-in is broken.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Cache-Control: private, no-store:&lt;/b&gt; signed-in pages are never cached at the edge or shared between guests. Trade-off: no edge caching, so pages are slower for guests far away." style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12;html=1;fillColor=#f7f7ff;strokeColor=#b9b9e6;dashed=1;dashPattern=4 4;fontColor=#1c1c1c;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="20.0" y="1805.0" width="700.0" height="244" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>